{{- /* The home feed, owned rather than inherited.

Forked from Hugo's embedded rss.xml, which sorts by Hugo's default page order:
any page with a nonzero `weight` sorts ahead of every page without one,
regardless of date. The governance documents carry `weight` to order the list
page, so they led the feed, three of them stamped year 0001 (issue #54).

Three changes from the embedded template, and no others:

  1. Page selection is explicit — dated pages only, newest first — instead of
     site.RegularPages in default order.
  2. The branches for site.Params.author and site.Copyright are omitted. None
     is set, so this emits the same channel the embedded template does. Set
     either one and this template must grow the branch back.
  3. No lastBuildDate. It was the only consumer of the hand-written `lastmod:`
     that every note carried, and with those gone it would have reported the
     newest `date:` — a value that never moves again, which is worse than an
     absent optional element. Setting `enableGitInfo` would restore a real one,
     but it also needs `fetch-depth: 0` in pages.yml, or CI's depth-1 clone
     dates every file to the deploy commit.

Notices appear here with no expiry test, and that is deliberate. The listing rule
— every notices listing goes through notices-by-status.html — does not reach a
feed: a feed is an archive and items are never removed from one, which is why the
notices *section* feed was dropped (#55) rather than filtered. README's Feeds note
is the authority; this paragraph exists so a reader arriving here from the rule
does not read it as a bug (#80).

`[services.rss] limit` still applies. RSS is not a plain-text output format, so
this runs through html/template: the prolog needs `safeHTML` and the summary
needs `transform.XMLEscape | safeHTML`, or the feed is mangled. This file is
outside the `task prettier` glob — keep the trim markers deliberate by hand.
*/ -}}
{{- $pages := where site.RegularPages "PublishDate.IsZero" false -}}
{{- $pages = $pages.ByPublishDate.Reverse -}}
{{- $limit := .Site.Config.Services.RSS.Limit -}}
{{- if ge $limit 1 -}}
{{- $pages = $pages | first $limit -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- printf "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?>" | safeHTML }}
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
  <channel>
    <title>{{ .Site.Title }}</title>
    <link>{{ .Permalink }}</link>
    <description>Recent content on {{ .Site.Title }}</description>
    <generator>Hugo</generator>
    <language>{{ site.Language.Locale }}</language>
{{- with .OutputFormats.Get "RSS" }}
    {{ printf "<atom:link href=%q rel=\"self\" type=%q />" .Permalink .MediaType | safeHTML }}
{{- end }}
{{- range $pages }}
    <item>
      <title>{{ .Title }}</title>
      <link>{{ .Permalink }}</link>
      <pubDate>{{ .PublishDate.Format "Mon, 02 Jan 2006 15:04:05 -0700" | safeHTML }}</pubDate>
      <guid>{{ .Permalink }}</guid>
      <description>{{ .Summary | transform.XMLEscape | safeHTML }}</description>
    </item>
{{- end }}
  </channel>
</rss>
